A||N||6||David Bartlett||Cooling Fan - A way to trick it to turn on?||||1||
Z||000000||David Bartlett||09-29-2001||07:45 PM||||Ok I brought my engine temp gage right up almost into the red... and the darn cooling fan didn't turn on. Is this a problem?  Is there a way to turn it on.. as in trick the sensor?<P>Oh I have a 2.8 with NO AC.  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||ka4nkf||09-30-2001||12:18 AM||||The best thing you can do is get a 210 on and 200 off fan switch from rodney. I promise you it is great.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fierowrecker||09-30-2001||01:27 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by David Bartlett:<BR><B>Ok I brought my engine temp gage right up almost into the red... and the darn cooling fan didn't turn on. Is this a problem?  Is there a way to turn it on.. as in trick the sensor?<P>Oh I have a 2.8 with NO AC.  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>I have two questions...<BR>Did you have to stop for an extended time with the motor running?<BR>Did you change coolant resently?<BR>If it redlined in traffic, then get the low temp switch, but if you changed coolant, you need to burp the system...<BR>Otherwise, let us know more as to what and when...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000003||David Bartlett||09-30-2001||01:37 AM||||Yes, I redlined it... but I did not wait until the temperature light came on.  <P>No, I didn't stop running the engine while doing the test.. took about 10 minutes and no I havent changed the coolent since I got the car.||||reg||1
Z||000004||JetroGT||09-30-2001||08:00 AM||||Time for a power flush.||||reg||1
Z||000005||maryjane||09-30-2001||11:29 AM||||David, any time you have a cooling issue, check The Ogre's Cave first. He has done a LOT of research on this and has a large article on it. When the Cave opens, the menu on the left has a heading called coolant issues i think. Instructions are there for manual switches, lower temp switches and thermostats. Check it out, he knows what he's talkin about. I also agree with the above suggestion about flushing your system. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||09-30-2001||12:58 PM||||if the car wasn't moving,,,, the OE fan sensor will not activate until 235F. a lower temperature sensor will solve that.<P>the Heat Management section is only for use AFTER you are certain the system is clean and operating properly. If you haven't changed the coolant, then the previous owner probably didn't either... Odds are good there's not a bunch of air or crap in there....<P>Coolant filling procedures are in the engine section.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
